      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "These are made of chains of amino acids. They are water-soluble, meaning they dissolve easily in blood. However, they cannot pass through cell membranes. So, they bind to receptors on the cell surface. Examples include;"
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Peptide and protein hormones",
            "header": [
              "Hormone",
              "Source (Gland)",
              "Main Function"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Insulin",
                "Pancreas",
                "Lowers blood glucose levels."
              ],
              [
                "Glucagon",
                "Pancreas",
                "Raises blood glucose levels."
              ],
              [
                "Growth Hormone",
                "Anterior Pituitary",
                "Stimulates growth and cell reproduction."
              ],
              [
                "Oxytocin",
                "Hypothalamus (released by Posterior Pituitary)",
                "Stimulates muscle contractions during childbirth."
              ]
            ]
          }
